<title>UK: UK's Brown seeking long-term fiscal stability.</title>
<headline>UK's Brown seeking long-term fiscal stability.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Britain's new finance minister Gordon Brown said on Tuesday he wanted fiscal stability for the long-term.</p>
<p>&quot;I said right at the beginning of my term as Chancellor that I wanted to plan for the long-term, monetary stability for the long-term, hence my reforms of the Bank of England,&quot; he told BBC Radio.</p>
<p>&quot;There will be fiscal stability for the long-term and we will get the public finances sorted out,&quot; he added.</p>
</text>
